  "question_stem": "In a certain chemical reaction the amount, $x$ grams, of a substance is increasing. The differential equation satisfied by $x$ and $t$, the time in seconds since the reaction began, is $$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}x}{\\mathrm{d}t} = kx\\mathrm{e}^{-0.1t},$$ where $k$ is a positive constant. It is given that $x = 20$ at the start of the reaction.",
